From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0260: Goodix spot lit by the panel's local HBM

The matcher sees the finger but scores it low: Android lights the spot with
the panel's own local HBM (a 1000-nit white circle), not a white page.
SweetFramebuffer gets sweet_fb_dsi_seq(): a panel command sequence in the
qcom dtsi format sent command by command through the existing command-DMA
path (the one the brightness uses), under its lock, each logged with its
DMA-done result; nothing is sent while the panel is off. SweetQsee carries the
n7_38_0c_0a sequences from the Lunaris dtbo (local HBM normal white 1000 nit,
local HBM off to normal, global HBM on/off): ops 22/23 local HBM on/off,
24/25 global HBM on/off; kern.sweet_qsee_arg bit 8 (0x100) lights the spot
before ops 15 and 20 (three frames, 50 ms) and turns it off afterwards.
